# SDEMO: Quick Demo Deploy

## Objective

Get work-control live on a public URL (Railway) fast — for demo purposes.
No auth, no Supabase, no CI required. bun:sqlite in-process DB is acceptable
for demo (ephemeral data resets on restart, which is fine).

## Strategy

Switch nitro preset from `'bun'` to `'node-server'` (one line), deploy to
Railway free tier. WebSockets work on Railway. SQLite stays. No DB migrations
needed — schema is auto-applied at startup.

## Target platform

**Railway** — Node.js server, persistent process, WebSocket support, free tier.
NuxtHub/Vercel blocked by: bun preset + WS on Cloudflare Workers.

## Tasks

- [ ] SDEMO-T01-NitroPreset.pd        — change preset bun→node-server, verify build
- [ ] SDEMO-T02-RailwayDeploy.pd      — Railway project setup + env vars + deploy
- [ ] SDEMO-T03-DemoSeed.pd           — seed script: 1 chat + 1 epic + board state

## Definition of Done

- [ ] `https://<project>.railway.app` loads work-control
- [ ] User can type in chat → ROOT proposes epics → Accept → board shows tasks
- [ ] WS events flow (live board updates on task run)
- [ ] URL is shareable — accessible without login

## Out of scope

- Auth (S15)
- Supabase (S23)
- CI/typecheck (S14)
- Multi-user presence demo (S12 — works locally, skip for speed)

## App-agent protocol

All tasks follow `APP-AGENT-PROTOCOL.md`.
Code tasks use `templates/PD-APP-AGENT-BLOCK.md`.
